<item>
            <title>[PARQUET-431] Make ParquetOutputFormat.memoryManager volatile</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-431</link>
                <project id="12315521" key="PARQUET">Parquet</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Currently ParquetOutputFormat.getRecordWriter() contains an unsynchronized lazy initialization of the non-volatile static field &lt;b&gt;memoryManager&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Because the compiler or processor may reorder instructions, threads are not guaranteed to see a completely initialized object, when ParquetOutputFormat.getRecordWriter() is called by multiple threads.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This ticket proposes to make &lt;b&gt;memoryManager&lt;/b&gt; volatile to correct the problem.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="12931740">PARQUET-431</key>
